DRIFT found while implementing k151 (gpt-6-astra effort gate).

Langertha::Engine::OpenAI::_max_tokens_key (lib/Langertha/Engine/OpenAI.pm ~line 99-103) returns max_completion_tokens only for models matching /\Agpt-5/, else max_tokens. gpt-6-astra matches \Agpt-6, so it falls through to max_tokens.

gpt-6-astra is a reasoning model (like the gpt-5.x line) and rejects max_tokens with HTTP 400 ("Use max_completion_tokens instead") - same failure that motivated karr #55 for gpt-5.x.

Impact: CONDITIONAL. _max_tokens_key only fires when a max_tokens control is passed to chat_f OR get_response_size is truthy (OpenAICompatible chat_request/chat_stream_request lines ~323-325 / ~458-460). A plain chat with no response_size set does NOT hit it. But any gpt-6-astra call that sets response_size / max_tokens would 400.

Fix (surgical): widen the anchored prefix in _max_tokens_key from /\Agpt-5/ to /\Agpt-[56]/, extend its comment + the k55 pinning test. Verify gpt-6 uses max_completion_tokens on the OpenAI model page while here.

NOT fixed in k151 per scope (effort block + catalog only; temperature-gate deferred to k155). Completion-length sibling of the same "gpt-6 not covered by gpt-5 prefix gates" family.

